{"transcription":"The z score =

138-104/17= 34/17=2

This means that kaiden scored 2 standard deviations above the mean on the test. His score is much higher than the average test taker. He did a better job than most students who took the test. A z score of 2 is usually considered unusual. Around 95% of scores fall within 2 standard deviations of the mean. So having a z score of 2 is usually high and less common than an average score. Basically Kaiden score would be unusually high.","score":8}

{"transcription":"The payment method would be Categorical, the number of items purchased would be quantitative discrete, and the total transaction amount in dollars is quantitative discrete.

Payment method would be categorical as you cant add credit cards vs Debit cards. Number of items purchased would be quantitative discrete because you cant make half a purchase, you either buy something or you don't. Whole number in dollars would also be quantitative discrete because its whole dollars, no quarters so it would be written as whole numbers, no decimals.

Classifying variables is important before selecting statistical methods because you need to know if its something that needs to be categorized vs averaged or added up. For example what the most popular dog is in the U.S vs what the average GPA is at Harvard. They would be measured differently, so its important to understand the type of data you have to organize and interpret.","score":4.5}

